====Usage notes====
* For paler shades, German does not use ''pink'' but {{m|de|rosa}}.
* ''Pink'' is generally declined like a normal adjective: ''eine pinke Jacke'' (“a pink jacket”). Some prescriptive grammars and dictionaries like [[w:Duden|Duden]] state that declined forms are colloquial and that ''pink'' should be invariable (''eine pink Jacke''). However, such usage is very rare and would even strike a great deal of native speakers as ungrammatical. See the various corpora at [https://www.dwds.de/wb/pink www.dwds.de], which include hundreds of attestations for the declined forms, but at most a handful for invariable use in attributive position.<!-- I checked the entire list and found exactly two (as of March '19). Maybe there are one or two more. -->

